{"duration_api_ms":32127,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a6dab37d-e2e9-411f-aeb0-7b6994548e28","total_cost_usd":2.56173,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":306943,"cache_read_input_tokens":186250,"output_tokens":3446,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1454},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":306943,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":186250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90271},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3446,"cacheReadInputTokens":186250,"cacheCreationInputTokens":306943,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.56173,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1454,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `coder-1.json` for Jacqui Irwin and coded the one topic (`egi-draft-a1v2`) at **rung 2**, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\" The file has one row and was written with a single Write call; nothing has checked it yet.\n\n- **The record:** Irwin voted Aye on AB 1955 (2023-2024) at the Assembly vote on concurring in the Senate amendments, on 2024-06-27. That was the bill's final Assembly vote and it passed 61-16. She was in her current Assembly term then, so it is `in-term`. About 21% of members voting said No, so it is not near-unanimous.\n- **Why rung 2:** the operative Section 220.5 says schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require\" staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That is rung 2's clause.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required to disclose.\" Nothing in the bill orders staff to keep the information from parents, which is what rung 1 would need.\n- **Evidence:** two passages on the same instrument, the vote page and the chaptered bill text, both in `rests_on`. Because they are one record, the published tier would be `single-source`. There are no quotes and nothing in `needs_source`.\n\n**Calls a reviewer should check:**\n- **Preemption:** Section 220.5 binds local school districts, so it is close to the preemption rule (H12). I coded it `on-question` rather than `adjacent` because rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules. I also treated the bill as single-subject: its other sections (resources for parents of LGBTQ pupils, protection for staff from retaliation) concern the same pupil-rights subject.\n- **Which text she voted on:** the source notes that the April Assembly floor vote was on a different, earlier text. I relied only on the June concurrence vote, which was on the chaptered text.","ttft_ms":14804,"type":"result","duration_ms":34194,"uuid":"081bce6f-fab2-4fbd-9a3c-4da2c5fa54e4","ttft_stream_ms":1987,"time_to_request_ms":253,"first_content_frame_ms":1988,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
